{
  "sn35.63:0.1": "Linked Discourses 35.63 ",
  "sn35.63:0.2": "7. With Migajāla ",
  "sn35.63:0.3": "With Migajāla (1st) ",
  "sn35.63:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn35.63:1.2": "Then Venerable Migajāla went up to the Buddha … ",
  "sn35.63:1.3": "and said to him: ",
  "sn35.63:1.4": "“Sir, they speak of one who lives alone. ",
  "sn35.63:1.5": "How is one who lives alone defined? And how is living with a partner defined?” ",
  "sn35.63:2.1": "“Migajāla, there are sights known by the eye, which are likable, desirable, agreeable, pleasant, sensual, and arousing. ",
  "sn35.63:2.2": "If a mendicant approves, welcomes, and keeps clinging to them, ",
  "sn35.63:2.3": "this gives rise to relishing. ",
  "sn35.63:2.4": "When there’s relishing there’s lust. ",
  "sn35.63:2.5": "When there’s lust there is yoking. ",
  "sn35.63:2.6": "A mendicant who is fettered by relishing is said to live with a partner. ",
  "sn35.63:2.7": "There are sounds … smells … tastes … touches … ",
  "sn35.63:2.8": "There are ideas known by the mind, which are likable, desirable, agreeable, pleasant, sensual, and arousing. ",
  "sn35.63:2.9": "If a mendicant approves, welcomes, and keeps clinging to them, ",
  "sn35.63:2.10": "this gives rise to relishing. ",
  "sn35.63:2.11": "When there’s relishing there’s lust. ",
  "sn35.63:2.12": "When there’s lust there is yoking. ",
  "sn35.63:2.13": "A mendicant who is fettered by relishing is said to live with a partner. ",
  "sn35.63:2.14": "A mendicant who lives lik